The first elements of NATO forces participating in Noble Jump 2021 arrive in Romania on Tuesday by land, the Defense Ministry informed. Eight military convoys, made of 190 military and 120 military equipment entered Romania through Giurgiu border crossing point.
They will stay in Bucharest until Wednesday and will continue going toward the Joint National Training Center “Getica”in Cincu, Brasov county.
Noble Jump 2021 (NOJP 21) is a short term multinational notification exercise, planned and headed by the Joint Force Command in Naples, held over May 19-June 2, in Romania and Bulgaria.
