9cf3b5ef-5dcc-4e28-bec9-628546a41904,"European Union, NATO",3066253b-5fb8-5a4d-a2db-78d03603ec5d,politico,politico.eu,https://www.politico.eu/article/nato-allies-extend-stoltenbergs-term-as-secretary-general/,English,31-03-2020,trustworthy,"NATO Secretary-General Jens Stoltenberg is not obsolete.
The 29 allied countries on Thursday extended Stoltenberg’s term as NATO’s top political official for two more years, until September 30, 2022, ensuring a measure of stability at a time of tension in transatlantic relations and apprehension over Russia’s military assertiveness.
Stoltenberg, a former Norwegian prime minister, was scheduled to complete the more traditional four-year term in 2020. And the decision by allies to extend his mandate underscored the confidence he enjoys in the capitals of the major powers — Washington, Berlin, London and Paris.",NATO allies extend Stoltenberg’s term as secretary-general
447091a6-d9b5-4f63-8fd3-5cbb490cc58d,"Sputnik V, coronavirus, vaccination",bda5fcfa-c871-5e4e-a23d-02c3b13f5681,the independent,independent.co.uk,https://www.independent.co.uk/news/health/sputnik-covid-vaccine-delta-variant-b1874718.html,English,21-06-2021,trustworthy,"Become an Independent member to bookmark this article
