de915145-4fec-4fb2-a494-0cfba809c1e8,"NATO, Anti-Russian, Nuclear issues, Puppets",1931987e-a4e0-5937-bda1-e892e3ef8bc7,gloucestershire live,gloucestershirelive.co.uk,https://www.gloucestershirelive.co.uk/news/regional-news/bombers-flew-after-taking-raf-6044142,English,13-10-2021,trustworthy,"Where US bombers flew to after taking off from RAF Fairford
The aircraft took off from the Gloucestershire airbase today
Two B1-B Lancer bombers took off from RAF Fairford as part of a ""task force mission"" today.
The pair of US Air Force aircraft left the Gloucestershire airbase this morning (October 11) and headed for Lithuania.
They were deployed to Eastern Europe in support of U.S. European Command’s Bomber Task Force 22-1 mission series ahead of their hot pit refuelling at Spangdahlem Air Base, Germany.
READ MORE: Watch B1-B Lancer bomber take off from RAF Fairford on US Air Force mission
The B1-B bombers are from the 9th Expeditionary Bomb Squadron based at Dyess Air Forces Base, Texas.
A statement from the US Air Force reads: ""The BTF Europe series supports the European Deterrence Initiative and actively pursues opportunities to integrate with coalition forces throughout the U.S. Air Forces in Europe – Air Forces Africa theaters.
""Coalition JTACS from Lithuania and Air Force Special Operation Command’s 352nd Special Operations Wing at RAF Mildenhall, England, coordinated with the bomber aircrews and identified simulated ground targets.
""The mission focused on enhancing readiness and interoperability for the controllers responsible for coordinating airstrikes to support ground forces.
""Spangdahlem’s 52nd Fighter Wing executed a hot pit refuelling, employing the new Versatile Integrating Partner Equipment Refuelling (VIPER) kit.
""The VIPER kit system, an Agile Combat Employment capability, enables the bombers’ ability to land and operate from austere airfields at any forward staging location.""
Gen. Jeff Harrigian, USAFE-AFAFRICA commander, added: ""BTF rotations allow our coalition to closely integrate and employ new and advanced tactics across two continents.
""Our joint and multinational forces must be ready to respond to any threat in order to maintain the global security environment.""
