7640bb3d-7830-4d0c-ab24-4e0ba279e6a8,"War in Ukraine, Invasion of Ukraine, Sergei Lavrov, Nazi/Fascist, DNR, LNR, illegal annexation, Referendum, Manipulated elections/referendum, Kherson",2d1c761b-7166-53d3-ae7a-4ea97f4393a3,radiofreeeurope/radioliberty,rferl.org,https://www.rferl.org/a/ukraine-zelenskiy-russia-donbas/31396762.html,English,22-09-2022,trustworthy,"Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskiy says he is doing ""everything"" he can to end the war with Russia-backed separatists but that peace and control of territory in the so-called Donbas depends ""90 percent"" on Russian President Vladimir Putin.
Speaking in an interview with a Ukrainian TV channel excerpted on August 5, he also said preparations were being made for a meeting with the Russian leader.
Zelenskiy said he ""really wants"" the conflict to end.
""Unfortunately, not everything depends on me,"" Zelenskiy said. ""I believe and don't hide it at all -- and the president of the Russian Federation knows my opinion -- today 90 percent of success in the return of the Donbas, peace in Ukraine, the de-occupation of our territories, depends on one person.""
