3f967233-a08f-4c81-8c97-71091bdbce13,"Donetsk, Provocation, Chemical weapons/attack",a471bf3d-29b4-498d-983e-5546deb94eb2,rossa primavera,eu.eot.su,http://eu.eot.su/2018/12/10/ukrainian-military-brings-drones-to-gorlovka-for-chemical-weapons-provocation/,English,09-12-2018,disinformation,"10.12.2018, Donetsk.
The Ukrainian military delivered a large consignment of drones to the region of Gorlovka, and they may be used in a provocation with chemical weapons, said the Donetsk People’s Republic (DPR) People’s Militia Press Secretary Daniil Bezsonov on December on 9, the Militia official site reports.
According to Bezsonov, the DPR intelligence services have obtained reliable information about the arrival of a railroad echelon with numerous armed drones to the region of Gorlovka. Part of drones was produced by Ukraine in collaboration with Turkey, and they are able of carrying payloads of up to 70 kg. The Ukrainian authorities bragged recently about the procurement of these drones.
Bezsonov added, “New armed drones will be used in carrying out a provocation in Donbass, in staging an air raid on the DPR’s strategically important infrastructure.”
The intelligence services report that Ukrainian and British military personnel prepared some staged videos intended for publication in the media following a provocation with chemical weapons. The fake is to prove the DPR People’s Militia involvement in using drones carrying chemical weapons.
Under the Minsk Joint Centre for Control and Coordination agreement, only OSCE observers are authorized to use drones along the line of contact in Donbass.
Source: Rossa Primavera News Agency",Ukrainian military brings drones to Gorlovka for chemical weapons provocation
437a0907-20ce-4a4b-aa3f-646a9d18e6ed,Sputnik V,33e8727c-571d-565d-be5b-f2a257293434,radiofreeeurope/radioliberty,rferl.org,https://www.rferl.org/a/ukrainian-parliament-bans-approval-of-russian-covid-19-vaccines/31076443.html,English,29-01-2021,trustworthy,"Lawmakers in Ukraine's parliament have overwhelmingly voted to ban the approval of vaccines made in Russia.
At the same time, the parliament on January 29 eased the process for registering vaccines from the United States, the European Union, China, India, and Mexico.
Ukraine has so far not started vaccinating its citizens.
The government has said it expects to receive 100,000 to 200,000 doses of the vaccine made by Pfizer Inc and Germany's BioNTech under the global COVAX initiative in February.
Authorities have repeatedly said Kyiv will not approve or use vaccines from Russia, with which the country’s ties are strained over the illegal annexation of Ukraine's Crimea in 2014 and its ongoing support to separatists in eastern Ukraine. The conflict has killed more than 14,000 people.
""One political force just created some hysteria over the registration of the Russian vaccine,"" Ukraine's Health Minister Maksym Stepanov told a televised briefing.
""I'll say this once: You can be hysterical for a very long time, no one will register the Russian vaccine in the country.""
The Health Ministry has recorded a steady decline in new infections, deaths, and hospitalizations in recent weeks.
More than 1.2 million coronavirus cases have been recorded since last March. More than 22,000 people have died from the virus.",Ukrainian Parliament Bans Approval Of Russian COVID-19 Vaccines
3f967233-a08f-4c81-8c97-71091bdbce13,"Donetsk, Provocation, Chemical weapons/attack",33f08510-73a9-49d7-aa2d-3d7e49034a78,tass,tass.com,http://tass.com/world/1035166,English,09-12-2018,disinformation,"DONETSK, December 9. /TASS/. A big number of assault drones that can be used to stage provocations with chemical weapons have been delivered by Ukrainian troops to an area near Gorlovka, Daniil Bezsonov, a spokesman for the defense ministry of the self-proclaimed Donetsk People’s Republic (DPR), on Sunday.
""We have received reliable reconnaissance data that a great number of assault drones of the Warmate-1 and Bayraktar types have been delivered by railway transport to the Gorlovka direction. Drones of the later type, manufactured jointly by Turkey and Ukraine, are capable of carrying of up to 70 kilograms. The Ukrainian authorities have recently boasted of buying drones of this type,"" the Donetsk News Agency quoted him as saying.
According to Bezsonov, these drones are meant to be used to stage provocations in Donbass and attack vital facilities in the DPR. ""Apart from that, the Ukrainian and British military have prepared video materials based on computer graphics to be released in media outlets after a chemical provocation. The fake videos are to serve as evidence of alleged use of unmanned aerial vehicles with chemical weapons by DPR servicemen,"" he said.
Under the agreements reached at the Minsk talks of the Contact Group, only monitors of the OSCE Special Monitoring Mission are allowed to use unmanned aerial vehicles in the areas adjacent to the contact line in Donbass.",DPR’s reconnaissance spots assault drones at Ukrainian troops’ positions in Donbass
